V: Kenyan Primary School Management System (SaaS Architecture Blueprint)
System Administrator, Edge Hardware Views, and Exhaustive Core Production Database Schema

7. System Administrator / SaaS Root Module (The Super Platform View)
------------------------------------------------------------------

This module sits above individual schools. It is the centralized multi-tenant panel
used by your core engineering team to manage subscriptions, monitor system health,
and onboard new institutions.

Page 7.1: Global Multi-Tenant Operations Center
- RBAC Scope: Accessible strictly by global SaaS-SuperAdmin. Completely hidden from
  individual school headteachers.
- UI Components:
  • Global Health Tiles: Total Active Tenant Schools, Aggregated Global Monthly
    Recurring Revenue (GMRR), System-Wide API Success Rate (M-Pesa/SMS Gateways),
    and Database Storage Overhead (GB).
  • Tenant Monitoring Grid: A data table tracking registered schools, their active
    license tier (Basic, Standard, Premium Enterprise), their current subscription
    status (Active, In Arrears, Suspended), and their cumulative student data footprint.
  • Action UI Assets: A contextual action dropdown next to each tenant row providing
    actions: [Suspend Tenant Access], [Force Database Schema Migration], or
    [Impersonate School Admin Profile] (for debugging support issues).

Page 7.2: Universal KICD Matrix Configurator
- UI Components:
  • Tree-View Hierarchy Node Editor: Allows global admins to modify curriculum models
    down to specific sub-strand levels when the Ministry of Education issues circulars.
  • Input Fields: Add New Subject Group, Map Outcome Descriptors, and Set National
    Weightings Configuration (e.g., KPSEA 40%).
  • Universal Propagate Button: A protected action trigger component labeled Deploy
    Curriculum Update System-Wide. Clicking it triggers a background database migration
    that seamlessly injects the updated matrix schemas across all tenant schemas
    without clobbering existing school assessment logs.

8. Physical Edge Hardware Views (The Security Turnstile Component)
------------------------------------------------------------------

For premium schools implementing physical biometric gates or RFID student badges,
this interface runs locally on low-cost hardware edge displays (e.g., a wall-mounted
7-inch tablet or Linux micro-panel attached to an entrance gate turnstile).

Page 8.1: Real-Time Gate Check-In/Check-Out Console
- Hardware Runtime Environment: A specialized local UI running on a Chromium kiosk
  window or a C++ embedded screen application connected via WebSockets or MQTT to
  the central cloud services.
- UI Layout States:

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|                  🔒 GATE 1 ENTRANCE                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                         |
|         [  STUDENT BADGE SCANNER ACTIVE...  ]           |
|                                                         |
|  STATUS MONITOR:                                        |
|  +---------------------------------------------------+  |
|  |  🟢 TAP RECEIVED AT 07:12:43 AM                   |  |
|  |  Name: Brian Omondi                               |  |
|  |  Admission ID: ADM-2024-4112                      |  |
|  |  Grade Block: Primary 4 East                      |  |
|  +---------------------------------------------------+  |
|                                                         |
|  >> DOWNSTREAM ACTION: Triggering Parent WhatsApp...    |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

- UI Workflow Actions:
  1. The device waits in a blank, high-contrast idle state reading input from an
     attached USB RFID card scanner or optical biometric thumbprint array.
  2. Upon a successful localized read event, the hardware client posts the numeric
     hardware signature token over a persistent WebSocket pipe.
  3. The UI instantaneously displays the student's profile thumbnail photograph
     alongside a large green indicator band labeled Access Granted or a red band
     labeled Contact Administration (Fee Arrears Gate Lockout Rule).
  4. Concurrently, a background execution hook passes a processing ticket to the
     communication engine, deploying an instant message notification card to the
     parent's phone interface.

9. The Exhaustive Core Production Database Schema (PostgreSQL)
-------------------------------------------------------------

To wire these multi-tenant views successfully without data leaks or runtime
collisions, here is the production-grade, relational data structure mapping
database schemas directly to the application views.

-- PostgreSQL Data Dictionary Blueprint for Kenyan Multi-Tenant Primary SaaS Engine

CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "uuid-ossp";

-- 1. TENANT MANAGEMENT
CREATE TABLE schools (
    tenant_id VARCHAR(50) PRIMARY KEY,
    school_name VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,
    subdomain VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    license_tier VARCHAR(30) DEFAULT 'STANDARD', -- BASIC, STANDARD, PREMIUM
    status VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'ACTIVE', -- ACTIVE, SUSPENDED, DEACTIVATED
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 2. ACADEMIC MATRIX SETUP (GLOBAL CONFIG MAP)
CREATE TABLE cbc_learning_areas (
    subject_id VARCHAR(50) PRIMARY KEY,
    subject_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL, -- e.g., Mathematics, Agriculture & Nutrition
    grade_level VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL     -- e.g., GRADE_1, GRADE_4, JSS_1
);

CREATE TABLE cbc_strands (
    strand_id VARCHAR(50) PRIMARY KEY,
    subject_id VARCHAR(50) REFERENCES cbc_learning_areas(subject_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    strand_name VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL
);

CREATE TABLE cbc_sub_strands (
    sub_strand_id VARCHAR(50) PRIMARY KEY,
    strand_id VARCHAR(50) REFERENCES cbc_strands(strand_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    sub_strand_name VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL,
    learning_outcome_rubric TEXT NOT NULL
);

-- 3. USER MANAGEMENT & RBAC
CREATE TABLE users (
    user_id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    tenant_id VARCHAR(50) REFERENCES schools(tenant_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    email VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    phone_number VARCHAR(15) NOT NULL, -- Format: 254XXXXXXXXX
    password_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    user_role VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL, -- SUPER_ADMIN, HEADTEACHER, BURSAR, TEACHER, PARENT
    is_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    CONSTRAINT unique_tenant_user_email UNIQUE(tenant_id, email)
);

-- 4. PUPIL & LEDGER RECORDS
CREATE TABLE students (
    student_id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    tenant_id VARCHAR(50) REFERENCES schools(tenant_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    admission_number VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    upi_nemis_number VARCHAR(50),
    full_name VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,
    grade_level VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
    stream_name VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL, -- e.g., Blue, West, Alpha
    parent_phone_number VARCHAR(15) NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    CONSTRAINT unique_tenant_adm_no UNIQUE(tenant_id, admission_number)
);

-- 5. REAL-TIME ASSESSMENT TRANS-LOGS
CREATE TABLE student_cbc_assessments (
    assessment_id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    tenant_id VARCHAR(50) REFERENCES schools(tenant_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    student_id UUID REFERENCES students(student_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    sub_strand_id VARCHAR(50) REFERENCES cbc_sub_strands(sub_strand_id),
    teacher_id UUID REFERENCES users(user_id),
    score_code VARCHAR(4) NOT NULL, -- EE, ME, AE, BE
    teacher_remarks TEXT,
    updated_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    CONSTRAINT unique_assessment_node UNIQUE(tenant_id, student_id, sub_strand_id)
);

-- 6. FINANCE EVENT LEDGERS
CREATE TABLE financial_invoices (
    invoice_id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    tenant_id VARCHAR(50) REFERENCES schools(tenant_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    student_id UUID REFERENCES students(student_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    fee_category VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL, -- TUITION, BOARDING, MEALS, TRANSPORT
    amount_invoiced NUMERIC(12,2) NOT NULL,
    amount_paid NUMERIC(12,2) DEFAULT 0.00,
    term_code VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL, -- e.g., 2026_TERM_1
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

CREATE TABLE mpesa_webhook_logs (
    transaction_id VARCHAR(50) PRIMARY KEY, -- Safaricom TransID
    tenant_id VARCHAR(50) REFERENCES schools(tenant_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    amount_received NUMERIC(12,2) NOT NULL,
    phone_number VARCHAR(15) NOT NULL,
    bill_reference VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL, -- Raw user input index
    reconciliation_status VARCHAR(30) DEFAULT 'PENDING', -- UNRESOLVED, AUTOFILLED, MANUAL
    raw_payload JSONB NOT NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 7. MULTI-TENANT SECURITY POLICY ARCHITECTURE
-- Enforce security layer partitioning directly at the engine base
ALTER TABLE users ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE students ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE student_cbc_assessments ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE financial_invoices ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE mpesa_webhook_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Sample policy template applied systematically to all operational data sets
CREATE POLICY tenant_isolation_policy ON students
    FOR ALL
    USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id', true));

-- Data Dictionary Entity Summary
-- schools                  : SaaS tenant root (one per school)
-- cbc_learning_areas       : Tier 1 KICD subjects (Mathematics, English, etc.)
-- cbc_strands              : Tier 2 themes per subject (Numbers, Measurement)
-- cbc_sub_strands          : Tier 3 topics per strand (Fractions, Decimals)
-- students                 : Tier 4 pupil records with tenant isolation
-- users                    : Staff/parent auth + RBAC roles per tenant
-- student_cbc_assessments  : CBC formative rubric entries (EE/ME/AE/BE)
-- financial_invoices       : Per-student fee structures and payments
-- mpesa_webhook_logs       : Safaricom C2B transaction audit trail (idempotent)

10. Execution Order: The Engineering Roadmap
--------------------------------------------

Now that the system is completely laid out across all backend architectures,
interface views, and data collections, your path to deployment runs through three
systematic execution sprints:

Sprint 1 (The Core Webhook Engine):
  Instantiate the PostgreSQL database infrastructure with Row-Level Security,
  build out the high-speed Go Ingest Gateway Layer, and deploy the Safaricom
  Daraja API endpoints. Confirm that an incoming raw payment simulation updates
  your ledger state correctly under load.

Sprint 2 (The Grading Grid Matrix):
  Construct the multi-subject data relational tables, build the PWA offline-first
  IndexedDB system for teachers, and lock down the single-tap grid view layouts.
  Run testing to ensure background synchronizations pass incremental diff arrays
  back to the central server smoothly.

Sprint 3 (The Downstream Notification Engine):
  Map the Java/Spring Boot communication processors to watch your database change
  streams, configure your Africa's Talking SMS fallback routines, and launch the
  low-bandwidth parent dashboard portals.

